Scenario: View no new support administrator contact emails for contact verified via provisioning
	Testing the ability to create a support administrator contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective new contact emails if the contacts do not yet exist in okta.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.user1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastName1}       |
	| Email Status  | UNVERIFIED                      |
	| Active        | true                            |
	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | MAILKRKRMAIL                    | |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki   | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                    | |
	| Name                  | Krmail - ${staticProjectName}   | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                    | |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                   | |
	| Status                | Active                          | |
	| Tier                  | T4                              | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com    | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Krmail - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Krmail - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Krmail - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support Administrator |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address Verified | false |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "pro.user1"
	And I click on the user with the name "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	# Necessary pause after sync button for email sync
	When I wait for "10" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view a support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay Provisioning" the recipient is "PRO ${staticContactLastName1}" with the email address "pro.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the message content contains the text "New Liferay Project Invitation - Krmail - ${staticProjectName}"

